  "reference_protocol": "Both public Core file modes compare return code, complete output, first diagnostic and persisted catalog/rows/integrity. The actual reference database enumerates identifiers as JSON strings; raw hex catalog bytes remain compared separately. Six cases hold the pinned SQLite writer open so newly inserted rows and a VIEW remain committed only in the live WAL. A fresh final seed differs from development. No target-specific answer route, mask, skip or output correction is used.",
  "implementation": [
    "IO page sources carry the actual database text-encoding cookie. Physical cell sizes and serial types are checked before TEXT fields are decoded into the existing UTF-8 Core value representation; numeric/NULL/BLOB fields retain their representation. Both catalog readers and both public file engines receive the actual cookie.",
    "BINARY has explicit UTF-16 LE/BE byte comparators; NOCASE/RTRIM retain their existing UTF-8 comparators. Compiler-owned connection hints select BINARY representation independently of explicit/declared COLLATE precedence. Physical index contents are independently validated in actual encoded order, then installed as an ordinary Core logical index.",
    "ScalarValue tracks current text representation and an encoded-byte cache for BLOB-to-TEXT casts. Private expression annotations carry real connection information; public SQL cannot call them. Scalar byte operations and CAST use actual database encoding. Function text results are normalized to the database encoding and UTF-16 TEXT casts truncate an odd byte as in the pinned engine.",
    "Name-only ORDER BY metadata remains an independent component; execution additionally maps BINARY to the actual connection encoding. The old universally quantified name-binding collation theorem is retained with a new literal-extraction proof for two- and three-argument annotations.",
    "The UTF-8 field path returns its original field list directly. UTF-16 writes remain explicitly rejected before mutation: this checkpoint does not silently rewrite their encoding or publish unsupported data."
  ],
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned src/utf.c sqlite3VdbeMemTranslate for endian/surrogate and odd-byte conversion; src/main.c BINARY byte comparison; src/vdbemem.c sqlite3VdbeMemCast TEXT even-length rule; src/vdbe.c OP_Function asserts text result encoding equals the connection encoding. Executable oracle controls are retained.",
  "proof_scope": "Registered component theorems retain UTF-8 input/byte/field and comparator paths, prove that encoded index ordering permutes all original expected key/rowid entries, retain the ordinary UTF-8 checked-index factory, preserve unencoded ORDER BY metadata and retain the exact production Runtime.Record/reference IO equality. The original name-binding collation theorem remains universally quantified. No complete Unicode translation, full SQLite equivalence or unbounded concurrency theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh survey share a generator and named feature families. Ten failures remain: triggers, WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys, partial indexes and expression indexes in both file modes. Passing the UTF-16 probe does not establish complete encoding support or a global compatibility percentage.",
